q q 1 0 0 1 60 747.8898 cm .039216 .133333 .25098 rg BT/F2 24 Tf 0 4 TD (History and Introduction of BLW)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 715.8898 cm .784314 .662745 .431373 rg BT/F2 13 Tf 0 4 TD (Part 2: Modernization and Milestones)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 566.8898 cm .172549 .243137 .313725 rg BT 5.085732 Tw/F1 12 Tf 0 121 TD (As the technological requirements of Indian Railways evolved, DLW continuously)Tj 2.155963 Tw 0 -19 TD (upgraded its manufacturing processes. In August 1999, the unit manufactured its first)Tj .650508 Tw T* (High Horse Power \(HHP\) diesel locomotive \(WDG-4\) under technology transfer. By April)Tj .888256 Tw T* (2002, the first fully in-house built 4000 HP WDG-4 locomotive was rolled out, marking a)Tj 3.251236 Tw T* (major milestone in high-power freight traction. This transition laid the foundation for)Tj 3.96737 Tw T* (developing complex drive systems, high-efficiency engines, and computer-controlled)Tj 0 Tw T* (mechanics.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 399.8898 cm .172549 .243137 .313725 rg BT .389815 Tw/F1 12 Tf 0 140 TD (A historic transformation occurred in the late 2010s. In alignment with the Government of)Tj 5.151959 Tw 0 -19 TD (India's mission for 100% electrification of the railway network, DLW successfully)Tj .493732 Tw T* (transitioned from manufacturing diesel locomotives to high-power electric locomotives. In)Tj -.12157 Tw/F2 12 Tf T* (February 2017)Tj/F1 12 Tf (, the first electric locomotive, a passenger class )Tj/F2 12 Tf (WAP-7)Tj/F1 12 Tf (, was turned out. In)Tj 1.370299 Tw T* (March 2018, the facility achieved a world-first by successfully converting two old diesel)Tj 3.167066 Tw T* (locomotives \(WDG3A\) into a single high-capacity electric locomotive \(WAGC3\). This)Tj .341781 Tw T* (achievement was repeated in December 2018 by converting two HHP diesel locomotives)Tj 0 Tw T* (into a WAG11 electric locomotive.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 232.8898 cm .172549 .243137 .313725 rg BT .648299 Tw/F1 12 Tf 0 140 TD (Recognizing this shift, in December 2020, the Ministry of Railways officially renamed the)Tj 4.979159 Tw 0 -19 TD (facility to )Tj/F2 12 Tf (Banaras Locomotive Works \(BLW\))Tj/F1 12 Tf (. In December 2023, the 10,000th)Tj 2.012299 Tw T* (locomotive manufactured by BLW was flagged off by the Hon'ble Prime Minister, Shri)Tj -.083674 Tw T* (Narendra Modi. In March 2025, BLW achieved its highest-ever single-month production of)Tj .573959 Tw/F2 12 Tf T* (61 electric locomotives)Tj/F1 12 Tf (, culminating in a record )Tj/F1 12 Tf[-7828.8308]TJ ( manufactured during)Tj .234299 Tw 0 -38 TD (locomotives. This level of production highlights the efficiency of BLW's assembly lines, its)Tj 0 Tw 0 -19 TD (advanced scheduling models, and the coordination of its engineering team.)Tj ET Q q .039216 .133333 .25098 rg BT/F2 8.5 Tf 54 795 TD (BANARAS LOCOMOTIVE WORKS \(BLW\), VARANASI)Tj ET .419608 .447059 .501961 rg BT/F1 8.5 Tf 379.4745 795 TD <53554d4d455220494e5445524e53484950205245504f525420972032303236>Tj ET .898039 .886275 .862745 RG .75 w 54 788 m 541 788 l S 54 52 m 541 52 l S BT/F1 8.5 Tf 54 38 TD <4954202620454450204465706172746d656e74209720566f636174696f6e616c20547261696e696e672050726f6a656374>Tj ET BT 492.7965 38 TD (Page 5 of 25)Tj ET Q Q
