q q 1 0 0 1 60 747.8898 cm .039216 .133333 .25098 rg BT/F2 24 Tf 0 4 TD (Loco Testing Shop \(LTS\))Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 715.8898 cm .784314 .662745 .431373 rg BT/F2 13 Tf 0 4 TD (Part 2: Electrical and High-Voltage Inspections)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 623.8898 cm .172549 .243137 .313725 rg BT 2.576759 Tw/F1 12 Tf 0 64 TD (Electrical testing is divided into low-voltage wiring checks and high-voltage functional)Tj .774359 Tw 0 -19 TD (testing. These steps ensure insulation integrity and proper subsystem communication. A)Tj 3.510359 Tw T* (single error in cable connections could damage expensive transformer or converter)Tj 0 Tw T* (components, making this phase critical for the locomotive's electronic systems.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 494.8898 cm .172549 .243137 .313725 rg BT 4.572399 Tw/F2 12 Tf 0 102 TD (Continuity and Megger Testing:)Tj/F1 12 Tf ( Before the locomotive is energized, technicians)Tj 2.70469 Tw 0 -19 TD (conduct insulation resistance tests using a Megger. This test checks the low-voltage)Tj .200299 Tw T* (control circuits and high-voltage power cables against the locomotive body. It verifies that)Tj 1.773959 Tw T* (no cable insulation has been damaged during assembly, preventing short-circuits. Any)Tj .04069 Tw T* (drop in insulation resistance below standard limits requires immediate isolation and wiring)Tj 0 Tw T* (review.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 346.8898 cm .172549 .243137 .313725 rg BT 1.776359 Tw/F2 12 Tf 0 121 TD (Auxiliary and Propulsion Subsystem Checks:)Tj/F1 12 Tf ( Once the continuity checks pass, the)Tj 4.649299 Tw 0 -19 TD (control voltage \(110 V DC battery power\) is switched on. Diagnostic software is)Tj 2.536299 Tw T* (connected to the vehicle control unit \(VCU\) to check auxiliary subsystems. Next, the)Tj 2.518639 Tw T* (pantograph is raised to draw 25 kV AC from the OHE line. The main transformer is)Tj 1.481299 Tw T* (energized, and the converters are started to verify auxiliary systems like traction motor)Tj .914759 Tw T* (blowers \(TMB\), transformer oil pumps, and air compressors. Technicians monitor phase)Tj 0 Tw T* (voltages, frequencies, and current draws to ensure balanced and stable operations.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 236.8898 cm .172549 .243137 .313725 rg BT 1.482359 Tw/F2 12 Tf 0 83 TD (Pantograph Functionality:)Tj/F1 12 Tf ( The pantograph's mechanics are tested to ensure it raises)Tj 2.202299 Tw 0 -38 TD (lower\). Technicians also check the contact pressure against the OHE wire to prevent)Tj .40069 Tw 0 -19 TD (contact loss or excessive wear, which prevents overhead line damage during high-speed)Tj 0 Tw T* (travel.)Tj ET Q q .039216 .133333 .25098 rg BT/F2 8.5 Tf 54 795 TD (BANARAS LOCOMOTIVE WORKS \(BLW\), VARANASI)Tj ET .419608 .447059 .501961 rg BT/F1 8.5 Tf 379.4745 795 TD <53554d4d455220494e5445524e53484950205245504f525420972032303236>Tj ET .898039 .886275 .862745 RG .75 w 54 788 m 541 788 l S 54 52 m 541 52 l S BT/F1 8.5 Tf 54 38 TD <4954202620454450204465706172746d656e74209720566f636174696f6e616c20547261696e696e672050726f6a656374>Tj ET BT 488.0705 38 TD (Page 21 of 25)Tj ET Q Q
